WEBVTT

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:13.200
In this video you embroider a label for things you have sewn: “Made with love” in an arc, with a name underneath.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:18.839
Click “New” on the left and then “Text” above the canvas.

00:00:18.839 --> 00:00:22.900
The text is already selected, so just start typing.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.800
Red means: too wide for the hoop.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.720
We will fix that in a moment with the font and the height.

00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:39.241
A click on the font opens the list, and every font shows your text right away.

00:00:39.241 --> 00:00:43.348
Grey means a letter is missing, the Ä for example.

00:00:43.348 --> 00:00:47.866
On the right it says which height the font is made for.

00:00:47.866 --> 00:00:49.673
I will take Excalibur.

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:54.373
The height is that of the capital letters.

00:00:54.373 --> 00:00:58.065
Nine millimetres, and it all fits the hoop.

00:00:58.065 --> 00:01:03.647
The green strip under the slider shows where the font looks good.

00:01:04.733 --> 00:01:08.742
Now for the arc: shape “Arc on top”.

00:01:08.742 --> 00:01:12.973
The radius sets how strongly it bends.

00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:20.858
Under “More”, a little more letter spacing gives the letters some air.

00:01:20.858 --> 00:01:23.187
And a dark blue with it.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:29.635
A second click on “Text” puts the next lettering right underneath.

00:01:29.635 --> 00:01:36.020
For the name I take a script font, Pacificlo, twenty millimetres high, in pink.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:42.920
The nice part: a lettering stays text.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:47.258
Double-click it, and Frieda becomes Emma.

00:01:47.258 --> 00:01:50.220
Font, thread and place stay.

00:01:51.333 --> 00:01:59.133
The space bar shows you how the machine stitches: first the blue arc, then the name.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:05.733
You save on the left, like any design.

00:02:05.733 --> 00:02:07.800
Your label is done.
